0.1.0
* initial implementation
* StdRESTful service (user.grafana.GrafanaCloud) publishes archive/loop
  records to Grafana Cloud over OTLP/HTTP (JSON encoding), with station,
  model, and unit_system published as static resource attributes and
  observations named per the weewx_<observation>_<unit> convention (e.g.
  outTemp in Celsius becomes weewx_outdoor_temperature_celsius)
  Basic auth (instance_id/api_key), configurable unit_system conversion,
  binding (loop/archive), skip_fields, and per-observation name/unit
  overrides via [[[inputs]]] (as in weewx-mqtt)
* bin/user/grafana_backfill.py: standalone CLI that extracts historical
  archive data up to a given point in time and writes it in OpenMetrics
  format, using the same naming/labels as the live uploader, ready for
  'promtool tsdb create-blocks-from openmetrics' + 'mimirtool backfill'
* bin/user/grafana_metrics.py: naming/unit/payload logic shared by both